{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Run a world frame by frame, with schedules for startup, a fixed timestep and each frame, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with states that switch systems on and off."}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" owns a world and a set of schedules, each named by a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":". You add","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"systems to the schedules by label, then call ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation\/update(elapsed:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" once a frame with the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"time that passed. The simulation decides which schedules run:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/startup"},{"text":" runs once, before the first frame.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/fixedUpdate"},{"text":" runs once for every fixed timestep of time that has passed, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"physics and other rate-sensitive rules advance by the same amount each run, however uneven the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"frames are.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/update","isActive":true},{"text":" runs once a frame.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The examples throughout this module use these components, resources and systems:"}]},{"code":["struct Position: Component { var x: Double }","struct Velocity: Component { var dx: Double }","struct FixedSteps: Resource { var count = 0 }","enum GameState: States { case menu, playing, paused }","","\/\/\/ Moves each entity by its velocity over one fixed timestep.","@System","struct Physics {","    func run(_ movers: Update<Position>.Over<Velocity>, _ fixedTime: ResourceReader<FixedTime>) {","        let seconds = fixedTime.value.timestep \/ .seconds(1)","        movers { position, row in","            position.x += row.components.dx * seconds","        }","    }","}","","\/\/\/ Counts the runs of the schedule it is in.","@System","struct CountSteps {","    func run(_ steps: ResourceWriter<FixedSteps>) {","        steps.value.count += 1","    }","}","","\/\/\/ Spawns a ball at the origin.","@System","struct SpawnBall {","    func run(commands: inout Commands) {","        commands.spawn(Position(x: 0), Velocity(dx: 64))","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The following example runs ","type":"text"},{"code":"Physics","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on a fixed timestep of 1\/64 second, the default. A frame","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of 50 milliseconds covers three whole timesteps, so the ball moves three times:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["var world = World()","let ball = world.spawn(Position(x: 0), Velocity(dx: 64))","","var simulation = Simulation(world)","simulation.add(to: .fixedUpdate) { Physics() }","simulation.update(elapsed: .milliseconds(50))","","print(simulation.world[Position.self, of: ball])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 3.0)\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"States","anchor":"States"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A state type is a type, usually an enumeration, that conforms to "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/States"},{"type":"text","text":": the screens of a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"game, or the phases of a simulation. Add one to a simulation with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation\/add(state:)"},{"type":"text","text":". The simulation keeps the current state in the "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/CurrentState"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"resource; to change it, a system sets "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/NextState"},{"type":"text","text":", and the change applies at the start of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"next frame. Entering, leaving and moving between states run schedules of their own,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/onEnter(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/onExit(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/onTransition(from:to:)"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/inState(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" makes a run condition that holds"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only in one state."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The following example spawns a ball on entering the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"playing"},{"text":" state and moves it only while the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"game is in that state:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["var simulation = Simulation()","simulation.add(state: GameState.menu)","simulation.add(to: .onEnter(GameState.playing)) { SpawnBall() }","simulation.add(to: .fixedUpdate) { Physics().runIf(inState(GameState.playing)) }","","simulation.update(elapsed: .milliseconds(50))","print(simulation.world.count)","\/\/ Prints \"0\"","","simulation.world.resources[NextState<GameState>.self].set(.playing)","simulation.update(elapsed: .milliseconds(50))","print(simulation.world.resources[CurrentState<GameState>.self].state)","\/\/ Prints \"playing\"","for (_, position) in simulation.world.query(Position.self) {","    print(position)  \/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 3.0)\"","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"role":"collection","modules":[{"name":"SimulationModule"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","title":"SimulationModule","symbolKind":"module","externalID":"SimulationModule"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation","doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel","doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/NonPositiveDuration"],"title":"Simulations","anchor":"Simulations"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Time","doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/FixedTime"],"title":"Time","anchor":"Time"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/States","doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/CurrentState","doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/NextState","doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/inState(_:)"],"title":"States","anchor":"States"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/simulationmodule"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/CurrentState":{"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"CurrentState","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/currentstate","abstract":[{"text":"A resource holding the state a simulation is in.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/CurrentState","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"CurrentState","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"CurrentState"},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/Simulation/add(state:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Adds a state type to the simulation, starting in the given state.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation\/add(state:)","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/simulation\/add(state:)","title":"add(state:)","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"add","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"S","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"state","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"S","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/ScheduleLabel/update":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/schedulelabel\/update","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The label of the schedule tha